  "body": "Requested by the user (2026-11-11): a library of **standard tool holders**, so a tool gets a real holder body without anyone drawing it.\n\n**What:** built-in **ER collet chuck** holders as revolved profiles, the format the tool's holder already uses (`crates/tools/src/holder_profile.rs` / `spun.rs`, editable since #475):\n- sizes **ER11, ER16, ER20, ER25, ER32 and ER40**;\n- each profile has the collet nut (outer diameter and length), the chuck body, and the gauge length to the nut face as an adjustable parameter.\n\nDimensions come from the public standards (ISO 15488 / DIN 6499 collet and nut sizes), recorded as typical values in the decision file. Original profiles; no vendor model is copied.\n\n**Behaviour:**\n- **In the tool editor,** pick a holder from the library; the profile drops into the tool's holder and stays editable.\n- **In the collision checks,** the holder is judged as the shape it is, through the existing holder-stack law. No new collision code should be needed.\n- **In MCP,** the tool's holder can be set to a library entry (or file an `MCP:` follow-up).\n\nEffort: high (holder geometry feeds the collision checks).\n\n**Done means:**\n- Every listed size can be picked, and its profile matches the recorded dimension table.\n- A test shows an ER32 nut colliding with a wall a cylinder holder of the shank's diameter would have missed, and the reverse case passing.\n- Undo restores the previous holder.\n\nPart of #743.\n",
